WEBVTT

00:16.808 --> 00:17.642
Here.

00:18.977 --> 00:21.396
Piisuke's birdfeed is 10,000 yen a month,

00:25.734 --> 00:28.403
leaving me with 2,000 yen to feed myself.

00:32.240 --> 00:35.285
Man, I wish I could eat
till I was full for once.

00:36.244 --> 00:38.872
But all my problems are gonna go away

00:39.831 --> 00:42.834
once I kill this Sakamoto guy.

00:43.960 --> 00:45.420
Right, Piisuke?

00:46.713 --> 00:50.925
I mean, one billion yen!
Imagine what we could do with all that.

00:51.926 --> 00:53.970
We might even be able to eat sushi!

02:25.186 --> 02:26.312
SAKAMOTO'S

02:26.396 --> 02:28.148
HEISUKE MASHIMO

02:28.231 --> 02:29.482
I gotta say,

02:30.483 --> 02:32.777
a <i>lot</i> of hit men are after that bounty…

02:33.528 --> 02:36.781
They're tearing the shop apart.

02:38.283 --> 02:40.660
<i>We'll need to do some major repairs.</i>

02:40.743 --> 02:42.871
But we don't have the money for that.

02:42.954 --> 02:43.955
So hopefully,

02:44.038 --> 02:46.708
we can win the tournament tomorrow
and it'll all work out.

02:46.791 --> 02:48.376
PAINTBALL TOURNAMENT
PRIZE: ¥1,000,000

02:48.459 --> 02:50.336
Hiya. Got a minute?

02:50.837 --> 02:51.921
Hello, how--

02:54.007 --> 02:56.551
Which one of you is Taro Sakamoto?

02:58.678 --> 03:00.471
HIT MAN
HEISUKE MASHIMO

03:00.555 --> 03:02.307
<i>Another hit man!</i>

03:02.390 --> 03:06.811
Hand him over without a fuss
and I'll let you go, fatty.

03:06.895 --> 03:09.147
<i>That's the Sakamoto you're looking for!</i>

03:09.230 --> 03:11.232
I'm just a part-timer here.

03:11.316 --> 03:13.192
I don't know a Taro Sakamoto.

03:13.985 --> 03:15.653
Wait, what?

03:16.863 --> 03:18.656
Isn't this Sakamoto's?!

03:18.740 --> 03:20.950
There are lots of shops with that name.

03:21.034 --> 03:24.454
Lots? Aw, man!

03:25.204 --> 03:26.497
You're cute.

03:27.081 --> 03:29.542
<i>This hit man's a moron.</i>

03:29.626 --> 03:32.337
<i>He doesn't even realize</i>
<i>that his target is right in front of him.</i>

03:32.420 --> 03:33.254
<i>Also…</i>

03:33.338 --> 03:34.964
<i>There are lots of them?!</i>

03:35.048 --> 03:35.882
SACAMOTO'Z

03:35.965 --> 03:37.759
<i>Wait. So that means…</i>

03:38.676 --> 03:40.762
<i>we won't get to eat sushi?</i>

03:40.845 --> 03:43.932
<i>No fair! That makes me so sad.</i>

03:44.015 --> 03:47.936
<i>His thoughts are so stupid and trivial!</i>

03:48.019 --> 03:50.104
<i>What a worthless mind to read…</i>

03:50.855 --> 03:54.651
But I asked this old lady on the street

03:54.734 --> 03:56.736
and she said Taro Sakamoto would be here…

03:56.819 --> 03:58.529
We told you, he's not here.

03:58.613 --> 04:00.615
Taro Sakamoto's a common name anyway.

04:00.698 --> 04:02.909
There must be two hundred million of them.

04:02.992 --> 04:04.410
Two hundred million?

04:04.911 --> 04:07.163
How am I supposed to find the right one?

04:07.247 --> 04:10.166
The train fees are gonna rack up…

04:11.501 --> 04:14.003
I don't even have enough money
for breakfast today.

04:52.542 --> 04:53.543
He's watching us.

05:03.928 --> 05:07.348
Thanks so much, you guys!

05:07.432 --> 05:09.934
Piisuke, you're welcome any day.

05:11.269 --> 05:13.938
We're so lucky they gave us pork buns,
huh, Piisuke?

05:15.231 --> 05:17.608
I didn't know
there were such dumb hit men.

05:17.692 --> 05:20.445
<i>Guys like that last surprisingly long.</i>

05:23.031 --> 05:26.075
Damn, I was really counting on that.

05:26.617 --> 05:29.620
I guess we're gonna be stuck
living in this tent for a while.

05:29.704 --> 05:33.207
Though this tent won't last much longer…

05:33.958 --> 05:36.711
Grandma back home gave it to me special,
and look at it now…

05:40.048 --> 05:44.510
Someday we're gonna make it big
and live in a huge house, Piisuke.

05:46.262 --> 05:49.098
You don't have what it takes
to be a hit man.

05:49.849 --> 05:52.477
Just quit already, jackass.

05:54.604 --> 05:58.524
I wanna show the guys who fired us
just how wrong they were.

06:19.295 --> 06:21.714
"Paintball Tournament"?

06:21.798 --> 06:23.966
A one million yen prize?!

06:24.634 --> 06:25.802
Holy smokes!

06:25.885 --> 06:28.638
With that much money,
I bet we could buy a condo!

06:29.806 --> 06:33.559
This is it, Piisuke. Luck is on our side!

06:38.940 --> 06:43.111
THE 52ND IKORAIZAKA SHOPPING STREET
PAINTBALL TOURNAMENT

06:46.697 --> 06:48.699
Let's win this thing.

06:48.783 --> 06:50.034
<i>One million yen…</i>

06:50.118 --> 06:53.204
Walkie-talkies for team communications
available over here.

06:53.996 --> 06:57.208
Wow, they have KIL2-Us.

06:57.792 --> 06:59.669
This equipment is legit!

07:00.128 --> 07:01.420
<i>Reel it in.</i>

07:02.630 --> 07:04.465
Good luck, guys!

07:04.549 --> 07:06.342
Lu, why aren't you playing?

07:06.425 --> 07:09.679
I'm not participating
in such a barbaric game.

07:09.762 --> 07:12.932
We're doing it to get enough money
to repair the shop.

07:13.015 --> 07:15.810
Well, I'm sure the two of us
can handle these amateurs.

07:15.893 --> 07:17.728
No, you can't do that.

07:17.812 --> 07:19.730
-Come on!
-Oh, jeez.

07:19.814 --> 07:24.110
Please? Please let me play!

07:24.193 --> 07:26.487
I'm telling you, you can't play alone!

07:26.571 --> 07:29.949
It's a team competition
requiring two to five people per team!

07:30.032 --> 07:31.826
Seriously?

07:35.621 --> 07:36.998
Piisuke?

07:42.628 --> 07:45.506
You guys have to help me!

07:45.590 --> 07:47.008
Get away from us!

07:47.091 --> 07:49.677
-Hey, let go!
-Pretty please!

07:49.886 --> 07:51.429
TEAM SAKAMOTO'S
TARO SAKAMOTO

07:51.512 --> 07:52.722
SHIN ASAKURA
HEISUKE MASHIMO

07:53.514 --> 07:56.017
Thanks so much, you guys.

07:56.100 --> 07:57.351
Damn it…

07:57.435 --> 07:58.769
<i>He's gonna slow us down.</i>

07:59.562 --> 08:01.898
Hello! Thank you for participating

08:01.981 --> 08:05.109
in the annual Ikoraizaka Shopping Street
Paintball Tournament!

08:05.193 --> 08:07.487
We'll be using paintball BB pellets.

08:07.570 --> 08:09.780
If you get shot, you're out of the game.

08:10.823 --> 08:13.367
The whole shopping street is your field.

08:13.451 --> 08:17.455
Shoot to your heart's content
and we'll clean up together afterwards.

08:17.538 --> 08:19.540
It's great that they do this every year.

08:19.624 --> 08:21.167
Sure is helpful.

08:21.250 --> 08:22.460
Now I get it.

08:22.543 --> 08:25.254
It also serves as community cleanup
for the neighborhood.

08:25.338 --> 08:27.965
<i>Prize money, cleaning… What a great event.</i>

08:29.467 --> 08:32.512
<i>Is everyone in position?</i>

08:32.595 --> 08:35.306
Hey, so, what am I supposed to do?

08:35.389 --> 08:36.891
Just shoot people!

08:36.974 --> 08:37.850
Got it!

08:38.351 --> 08:40.144
But don't shoot us teammates, okay?

08:40.228 --> 08:41.521
I'm not <i>that</i> dumb!

08:42.271 --> 08:43.773
What's with those guys?

08:43.856 --> 08:44.941
Rookies, right?

08:45.024 --> 08:46.442
<i>-And… begin!</i>
-They won't last--

08:52.240 --> 08:54.867
<i>Did he… shoot those guys?</i>

08:54.951 --> 08:57.286
What? She said "begin," right?

08:57.370 --> 08:59.497
<i>Starting off strong, it's Sakamoto's!</i>

08:59.580 --> 09:00.748
How did that happen?

09:00.831 --> 09:02.750
-The heck?
<i>-What a way to kick it off!</i>

09:02.833 --> 09:03.960
<i>How did he…</i>

09:04.835 --> 09:06.087
<i>Caught you off guard.</i>

09:12.802 --> 09:15.221
No hard feelings, Mr. Sakamoto.

09:20.351 --> 09:22.562
THESE ARE AIRSOFT GUNS

09:23.145 --> 09:25.064
Sakamoto's is crushing it!

09:25.147 --> 09:27.400
Looks like they're our top contender!

09:28.025 --> 09:29.068
<i>We've got this!</i>

09:30.027 --> 09:32.071
<i>Bulletproof glass for the shop,</i>

09:32.154 --> 09:34.907
<i>an expanded range of instant noodles…</i>

09:34.991 --> 09:37.285
<i>This is super fun!</i>

09:37.368 --> 09:39.912
<i>So this is what it's like to</i>
<i>have comrades.</i>

09:39.996 --> 09:44.500
<i>It's so nice to have pals</i>
<i>to watch your back…</i>

09:44.584 --> 09:47.211
<i>He thinks we're "pals" already?</i>

09:47.962 --> 09:50.548
By the way, you guys are really good.

09:51.048 --> 09:52.466
Are you guys professional…

09:52.967 --> 09:54.093
<i>He knows?</i>

09:54.677 --> 09:56.053
…paintball nerds?

09:56.137 --> 09:57.597
<i>Good thing he's dumb.</i>

09:58.639 --> 10:01.726
Okay. I'll be the decoy
and get up to the front line.

10:01.809 --> 10:03.728
Cover me, brothers!

10:03.811 --> 10:06.981
He's not a bad guy, I guess.

10:07.064 --> 10:10.985
Woo-hoo! Get 'em, legend!
Go, Taro Sakamoto!

10:11.068 --> 10:13.446
I love how your belly jiggles!

10:17.158 --> 10:19.368
Taro… Sakamoto?

10:29.253 --> 10:31.964
Nah, he looks nothing like this!

10:33.341 --> 10:35.551
That's Mr. Manager when he was thin!

10:35.635 --> 10:38.179
I like him better chubby.

10:38.262 --> 10:41.474
See? His glasses and hair
are the exact same--

10:45.353 --> 10:47.730
This doesn't look anything like you,
Mr. Sakamoto.

10:50.066 --> 10:51.442
Right?

11:09.377 --> 11:11.087
I don't like liars.

11:19.762 --> 11:21.597
Uh-oh! They were on a roll,

11:21.680 --> 11:25.518
but the members of Team Sakamoto's
are now turning on each other!

11:25.601 --> 11:26.936
How could you?

11:27.645 --> 11:29.188
I thought you were my pals.

11:31.774 --> 11:35.444
<i>That damn Lu.</i>
<i>She just couldn't keep her mouth shut.</i>

11:36.445 --> 11:37.530
Oh, well.

11:37.947 --> 11:41.117
Looks like I'm getting
both the prize and the bounty.

11:44.870 --> 11:46.080
Caught you off guard!

11:46.163 --> 11:47.415
Die, you suckers!

11:47.498 --> 11:50.418
<i>Whoa! Team Barbers, coming in strong!</i>

11:50.501 --> 11:52.336
Perfect timing.

11:54.588 --> 11:55.506
Ow!

11:56.841 --> 11:57.675
Argh!

11:59.635 --> 12:00.928
Over here, Piisuke!

12:08.102 --> 12:11.021
Airsoft guns are fun and all, but…

12:15.234 --> 12:16.444
<i>A real gun?!</i>

12:16.527 --> 12:18.320
…this is more my style!

12:30.499 --> 12:33.210
<i>From that distance, with that stance…</i>

12:34.253 --> 12:36.046
<i>Such a well-aimed headshot…</i>

12:38.132 --> 12:40.468
I guess it can't be that easy.

12:40.551 --> 12:42.136
Let's go farther, Piisuke.

12:43.220 --> 12:44.054
Hey, wait!

12:44.555 --> 12:46.557
Shin, we have to deal with this first.

12:50.978 --> 12:53.063
Man, who would've thought…

12:54.440 --> 12:56.734
our target would be right under our noses?

12:56.817 --> 12:58.444
We really are lucky!

12:58.944 --> 13:01.614
What is it, Piisuke?

13:04.617 --> 13:06.619
No, I'm not crying…

13:07.912 --> 13:10.623
I'm not sad at all.

13:12.958 --> 13:15.252
They're my enemies!

13:15.336 --> 13:16.378
You get it, right?

13:19.006 --> 13:20.049
Either way,

13:20.591 --> 13:22.426
this is something I have to do.

13:23.093 --> 13:26.931
I need to make my mark
as a freelance hit man!

13:28.098 --> 13:30.809
All right, the tournament
is coming to its climax!

13:31.477 --> 13:35.981
<i>Which team will win</i>
<i>and take home the prize?</i>

13:37.566 --> 13:40.486
He doesn't seem to be near.

13:40.569 --> 13:42.446
-I'll take a look around.
<i>-Stop.</i>

13:43.113 --> 13:45.658
<i>You need to be cautious</i>
<i>in battles with a sniper.</i>

13:46.242 --> 13:48.744
<i>First, you determine where they are.</i>

13:49.245 --> 13:53.541
<i>However, you must do so</i>
<i>without giving away your own position.</i>

14:06.845 --> 14:07.888
<i>A ricochet?</i>

14:09.473 --> 14:11.267
<i>Where is he shooting from?</i>

14:11.934 --> 14:13.477
<i>He knows our location?</i>

14:16.855 --> 14:18.232
Seriously, Piisuke?

14:20.025 --> 14:21.861
He dodged that one too?

14:22.444 --> 14:24.446
<i>Are you alright, Mr. Sakamoto?</i>

14:24.530 --> 14:26.907
You dodged that, huh? Pretty impressive.

14:28.242 --> 14:30.911
What are you talking about?
It was a random ricochet.

14:30.995 --> 14:32.288
Don't get smug.

14:32.371 --> 14:33.539
It wasn't random.

14:35.082 --> 14:37.793
His round had an absurd spin rate.

14:39.044 --> 14:42.381
<i>I think it was designed</i>
<i>specifically to ricochet.</i>

14:43.257 --> 14:46.468
<i>Wow. Didn't think you'd figure that out.</i>

14:47.469 --> 14:48.470
You're right.

14:48.554 --> 14:51.140
The rounds I use
are called triple-rebound rounds.

14:51.223 --> 14:54.560
<i>They're made to bounce</i>
<i>so you can't track the trajectory.</i>

14:54.643 --> 14:56.604
It's a special design.

14:58.355 --> 15:02.234
For someone who called us "pals,"
you have no problem with killing us.

15:02.318 --> 15:03.861
Don't be so naive.

15:04.403 --> 15:07.489
We're hit men before we're pals.

15:08.324 --> 15:10.618
Once I put my eye to the scope,

15:10.701 --> 15:12.453
it's just a matter of hit or miss.

15:12.536 --> 15:14.121
Nothing else.

15:40.064 --> 15:40.981
CONSTRUCTION ZONE

15:41.065 --> 15:44.151
Seriously? He won't even
let us catch our breath!

15:51.617 --> 15:52.993
They put up a good fight.

15:57.247 --> 15:58.874
<i>Ever since I was young,</i>

15:58.958 --> 16:01.460
<i>I've never been able</i>
<i>to measure up to my peers.</i>

16:04.546 --> 16:07.466
You're really no good at anything,
huh, Heisuke?

16:13.222 --> 16:14.890
<i>But somehow,</i>

16:14.974 --> 16:17.851
<i>I could keep pace</i>
<i>when it came to shooting.</i>

16:21.021 --> 16:24.108
<i>This is it! This has got to be my thing!</i>

16:24.984 --> 16:27.361
Hi, I'm the new hire, Heisuke Mashimo.

16:27.444 --> 16:29.655
My expertise is sniping.

16:29.738 --> 16:32.616
In the academy,
I focused on my sniping skills.

16:33.200 --> 16:35.619
I'll be the best sniper you've ever had.

16:35.703 --> 16:36.829
Nice to meet you all!

16:38.497 --> 16:40.249
What's wrong with you?

16:42.710 --> 16:46.880
What use would we have
for a guy who can only do one thing?

16:46.964 --> 16:47.798
ONE KILL PER DAY

16:47.881 --> 16:50.884
Did you think
you'd get to choose your tasks, rookie?

16:50.968 --> 16:52.177
Go, go!

16:52.261 --> 16:53.220
Kill 'em all!

16:55.639 --> 16:57.683
What're you doing, Mashimo?

16:57.766 --> 16:59.643
You can't even handle a knife?

17:01.937 --> 17:05.482
Mashimo, stop slowing us down!
I'm gonna kill you!

17:09.111 --> 17:10.362
I'm telling you.

17:10.446 --> 17:12.906
You really aren't cut out to be a hit man.

17:12.990 --> 17:15.617
Who cares if you can shoot
if that's all you can do?

17:15.701 --> 17:18.078
Just quit already, jackass.

17:20.831 --> 17:24.585
<i>Unable to fit in, I got fired from my job.</i>

17:26.378 --> 17:28.839
I'm so hungry. You too, Piisuke?

17:32.843 --> 17:36.847
"Taro Sakamoto… Bounty, one billion yen."

17:36.930 --> 17:38.265
WANTED: TARO SAKAMOTO

17:44.521 --> 17:45.564
This is it.

17:48.108 --> 17:53.781
I'm gonna prove to them
that I am an awesome sniper.

18:02.414 --> 18:05.918
I need to complete this hit to prove…

18:06.460 --> 18:07.503
<i>that I'm not--</i>

18:07.586 --> 18:10.714
Shut up already! Your mic is on.

18:11.882 --> 18:13.509
Dang, you heard all that?

18:14.134 --> 18:16.845
Who cares what other people think?

18:16.929 --> 18:18.305
What does it matter?!

18:20.015 --> 18:22.518
The person you need to prove yourself to

18:22.601 --> 18:26.063
is you, and only <i>you!</i>

18:29.650 --> 18:31.485
<i>When people get surprised,</i>

18:31.568 --> 18:33.654
<i>I can read their thoughts even from afar.</i>

18:36.740 --> 18:39.118
Well played.
Attacking me with your loud voice.

18:40.035 --> 18:41.870
I got a screechy ringing in my ear.

18:58.470 --> 18:59.763
<i>With a pebble?</i>

19:06.937 --> 19:08.480
<i>This guy's a monster…</i>

19:10.774 --> 19:14.403
<i>There's no way I could ever beat him…</i>

19:16.196 --> 19:17.281
PAINTBALL TOURNAMENT

19:17.364 --> 19:20.784
All day, we've watched teams fight
to survive this cutthroat game,

19:20.868 --> 19:23.787
and now, it has finally come to an end!

19:24.454 --> 19:27.958
The winner of this year's game is…

19:28.625 --> 19:31.503
Team Sakamoto's!

19:31.587 --> 19:32.462
WINNER'S PRIZE

19:32.546 --> 19:34.673
Way to go!

19:37.050 --> 19:40.304
Turns out, I'm not even a good sniper.

19:42.139 --> 19:43.974
Damn it all!

19:44.057 --> 19:46.059
Man, you cry a lot.

19:46.143 --> 19:47.644
Are you really a hit man?

19:47.728 --> 19:48.729
Shut up!

19:48.812 --> 19:51.982
It's not like you guys would know
what it feels like to be weak.

19:52.065 --> 19:53.066
Weak?

19:54.985 --> 19:58.488
Never have I fought such a skilled sniper.

19:58.572 --> 19:59.448
Not once.

20:12.878 --> 20:17.841
It's not like that's the nicest thing
someone has ever said to me!

20:18.342 --> 20:20.344
Stop crying about everything!

20:25.057 --> 20:26.058
Oh, the prize…

20:26.725 --> 20:27.893
Here's your share.

20:27.976 --> 20:29.686
I get to have some?

20:32.731 --> 20:34.399
Only 50 yen?!

20:35.692 --> 20:38.070
You wrecked half the town
with those ricochets.

22:09.995 --> 22:11.121
PAINTBALL TOURNAMENT
WINNER

22:11.204 --> 22:12.914
What a shame.

22:12.998 --> 22:16.376
You fought so hard to win,
but used all the money to fix up the town.

22:17.002 --> 22:17.919
Sorry.

22:18.003 --> 22:20.922
It's okay.
You're safe and that's what matters.

22:21.840 --> 22:24.426
Hey, how did you two meet?

22:24.509 --> 22:25.677
Huh?

22:25.761 --> 22:28.889
I can't imagine Mr. Sakamoto
asking someone out.

22:29.389 --> 22:31.058
Well, you know…

22:37.564 --> 22:39.357
Hi! May I help you?

22:44.237 --> 22:46.239
That'll be 1,063 yen.

22:52.245 --> 22:53.580
Is that blood on your shirt?

23:05.217 --> 23:06.051
Sir?

23:07.344 --> 23:08.261
Here,

23:09.513 --> 23:10.514
this is for you.

23:14.392 --> 23:17.646
He has a surprisingly pure heart.

23:21.691 --> 23:23.485
<i>Stop reading Aoi's mind.</i>

23:23.568 --> 23:24.402
Sorry, sir.

23:24.486 --> 23:25.904
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
